        "claim": "Uninstall removes the plugin directory only when removing index.js succeeded. If index.js is already gone and an empty plugin directory remains (for example after a partial uninstall or a manual delete), the empty directory is left and OpenCode loads it as a plugin with no index.js, which is the failure the comment says the code prevents. The old flat plugins/labdrian-runtime-parity.js left by a pre-upgrade install is also never removed by uninstall, so an upgraded install leaves an orphan file the overlay no longer tracks.",
